{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "EXO",
  "chapter": 30,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "EXO.30.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EXO.30.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And thou shalt make an altar to burn incense upon: ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "of",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " shittim wood shalt thou make it.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "EXO.30.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EXO.30.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A cubit ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "shall be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " its length, and a cubit its breadth; foursquare shall it be; and two cubits ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "shall be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " its hight: its horns ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "shall be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " of the same.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EXO.30.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EXO.30.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And thou shalt overlay it with pure gold, its top, and its sides round about, and its horns; and thou shalt make to it a crown of gold round about.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EXO.30.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EXO.30.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And two golden rings shalt thou make to it under the crown of it, by its two corners, upon the two sides of it shalt thou make ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": "; and they shall be for places for the staffs to bear it with.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EXO.30.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EXO.30.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And thou shalt make the staffs of shittim wood, and overlay them with gold.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EXO.30.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EXO.30.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And thou shalt put it before the vail that ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " by the ark of the testimony, before the mercy-seat that ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " over the testimony, where I will meet with thee.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EXO.30.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EXO.30.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Aaron shall burn upon it sweet incense every morning: when he dresseth the lamps, he shall burn incense upon it.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EXO.30.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EXO.30.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And when Aaron lighteth the lamps at evening, he shall burn incense upon it; a perpetual incense before the LORD, throughout your generations.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EXO.30.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EXO.30.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Ye shall offer no strange incense upon it, nor burnt-sacrifice, nor meat-offering; neither shall ye pour drink-offering upon it.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EXO.30.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EXO.30.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Aaron shall make an atonement upon the horns of it once in a year, with the blood of the sin-offering of atonements: once in a year shall he make atonement upon it throughout your generations: it ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " most holy to the LORD.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EXO.30.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EXO.30.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the LORD spoke to Moses, saying,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EXO.30.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EXO.30.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "When thou takest the sum of the children of Israel after their number, then shall they give every man a ransom for his soul to the LORD, when thou numberest them: that there may be no plague among them, when ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "thou",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " numberest them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EXO.30.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EXO.30.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "This they shall give, every one that passeth among them that are numbered, half a shekel, after the shekel of the sanctuary: (a shekel ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " twenty gerahs:) a half shekel ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "shall be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the offering of the LORD.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EXO.30.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EXO.30.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Every one that passeth among them that are numbered from twenty years old and above, shall give an offering to the LORD.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EXO.30.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EXO.30.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The rich shall not give more, and the poor shall not give less than half a shekel, when ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "they",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " give an offering to the LORD to make an atonement for your souls.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EXO.30.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EXO.30.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And thou shalt take the atonement-money of the children of Israel, and shalt appoint it for the service of the tabernacle of the congregation; that it may be a memorial to the children of Israel before the LORD, to make an atonement for your souls.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EXO.30.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EXO.30.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the LORD spoke to Moses, saying,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EXO.30.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EXO.30.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou shalt also make a laver ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "of",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " brass, and its foot ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "also of",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " brass, to wash ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "in",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ": ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " thou shalt put it between the tabernacle of the congregation and the altar, and thou shalt put water therein.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EXO.30.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EXO.30.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For Aaron and their sons shall wash their hands and their feet thereat:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EXO.30.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EXO.30.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "When they go into the tabernacle of the congregation, they shall wash with water, that they die not: or when they come near to the altar to minister, to burn offering made by fire to the LORD.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EXO.30.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EXO.30.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "So they shall wash their hands and their feet, that they die not: and it shall be a statute for ever to them, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "even",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to him and to his seed throughout their generations.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EXO.30.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EXO.30.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Moreover the LORD spoke to Moses, saying,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EXO.30.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EXO.30.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Take thou also to thee principal spices, of pure myrrh five hundred ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "shekels",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", and of sweet cinnamon half as much, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "even",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " two hundred and fifty ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "shekels",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", and of sweet calamus two hundred and fifty ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "shekels",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ",",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EXO.30.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EXO.30.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And of cassia five hundred ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "shekels",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", after the shekel of the sanctuary, and of olive-oil a hin:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EXO.30.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EXO.30.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And thou shalt make it an oil of holy ointment, an ointment compound after the art of the apothecary: it shall be a holy anointing oil.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EXO.30.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EXO.30.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And thou shalt anoint the tabernacle of the congregation with it, and the ark of the testimony,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EXO.30.27",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EXO.30.27",
      "verse": 27,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the table and all its vessels, and the candlestick and its vessels, and the altar of incense,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EXO.30.28",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EXO.30.28",
      "verse": 28,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the altar of burnt-offering with all its vessels, and the laver and its foot.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EXO.30.29",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EXO.30.29",
      "verse": 29,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And thou shalt sanctify them, that they may be most holy: whatever toucheth them shall be holy.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EXO.30.30",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EXO.30.30",
      "verse": 30,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And thou shalt anoint Aaron and his sons, and consecrate them, that ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "they",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " may minister to me in the priest's office.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EXO.30.31",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EXO.30.31",
      "verse": 31,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And thou shalt speak to the children of Israel, saying, This shall be a holy anointing oil to me, throughout your generations.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EXO.30.32",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EXO.30.32",
      "verse": 32,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Upon man's flesh shall it not be poured, neither shall ye make ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "any other",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " like it, after the composition of it: it ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " holy, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " it shall be holy to you.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EXO.30.33",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EXO.30.33",
      "verse": 33,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Whoever compoundeth ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "any",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " like it, or whoever putteth ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "any",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " of it upon a stranger, shall even be cut off from his people.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EXO.30.34",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EXO.30.34",
      "verse": 34,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the LORD said to Moses, Take to thee sweet spices, stacte, and onycha, and galbanum; ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "these",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " sweet spices with pure frankincense: of each shall there be a like ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "weight",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ":",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EXO.30.35",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EXO.30.35",
      "verse": 35,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And thou shalt make it a perfume, a confection after the art of the apothecary, tempered together, pure ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " holy:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EXO.30.36",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EXO.30.36",
      "verse": 36,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And thou shalt beat ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "some",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " of it very small, and put of it before the testimony in the tabernacle of the congregation, where I will meet with thee: it shall be to you most holy:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EXO.30.37",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EXO.30.37",
      "verse": 37,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "as for",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the perfume which thou shalt make, ye shall not make to yourselves according to its composition: it shall be to thee holy for the LORD.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EXO.30.38",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EXO.30.38",
      "verse": 38,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Whoever shall make the like to that, to smell thereto, shall even be cut off from his people.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
